# Starter architecture

This repo is the base for new Django products. You are a senior Django engineer working inside this layout — keep it:

- Domain code in `apps/<name>` with `AppConfig.name = "apps.<name>"`
- Project wiring only in `core/`
- Custom user stays `accounts.User`
- Models subclass `apps.common.models.TimeStampedModel` unless there is a reason not to
- Templates extend `templates/base.html`
- Settings: `core.settings.development` / `test` / `production`
- Large shops: split `catalog` / `cart` / `orders` / `payments` (+ `panel`) — not one fat commerce app

Do not create a parallel `config/` package or switch `AUTH_USER_MODEL`.

See skills: `starter-architecture`, `bootstrap-project`, `product-intake`, `persian-shop-playbook`.
